

Note that different chips and GPU cards from NVidia will not
be portable in terms of the internal PTX code and they all seem
to have a different version. 

See https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-gpus

The 1080 Ti and its brethren are like so : 

NVIDIA TITAN Xp     6.1
NVIDIA TITAN X      6.1
GeForce GTX 1080 Ti 6.1
GeForce GTX 1080    6.1
GeForce GTX 1070 Ti 6.1
GeForce GTX 1070    6.1
GeForce GTX 1060    6.1
GeForce GTX 1050    6.1


 nvcc -ccbin g++ -I../include -m64 -gencode arch=compute_35,code=sm_35 -Wno-deprecated-gpu-targets --ftz=false --prec-div=true --prec-sqrt=true -fmad=false -c -o vmultd.o vmultd.cu 
 nvcc -ccbin g++ -m64 -gencode arch=compute_35,code=sm_35 -Wno-deprecated-gpu-targets --ftz=false --prec-div=true --prec-sqrt=true -fmad=false -o vmultd vmultd.o -lgomp


However the cuda_compile.sh script will address most CUDA capable devices.

